Ladybird now negates HarfBuzz’s y offsets and advances, since its
glyph positions grow downward. Blink does the same, in
ShapeResult::ComputeGlyphPositions(), which stores each offset as
GlyphOffset(x_offset, -y_offset). And Gecko’s
gfxHarfBuzzShaper::SetGlyphsFromRun() subtracts the y offset from the
block position of each glyph. WebKit’s HarfBuzz ComplexTextRun keeps the
offsets y-up, like the CoreText glyph origins its ComplexTextController
takes on macOS.
